"1\n00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,229\nThe Learning Brain. Series 3: Generative AI\n\n2\n00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,225\nEpisode 8\n\n3\n00:00:07,305 --> 00:00:09,741\nThinking alongside AI\n\n4\n00:00:12,541 --> 00:00:20,995\nThree hundred and nineteen knowledge workers described nine hundred and thirty six real examples of using generative AI at work,\n\n5\n00:00:21,470 --> 00:00:24,040\nand how much critical thinking each one took.\n\n6\n00:00:24,665 --> 00:00:27,983\nAll of them used AI at work at least once a week.\n\n7\n00:00:28,153 --> 00:00:31,534\nTwo kinds of confidence pulled in opposite directions.\n\n8\n00:00:31,904 --> 00:00:34,824\nThe more people trusted the AI on a task,\n\n9\n00:00:35,045 --> 00:00:37,325\nthe less critical thinking they reported.\n\n10\n00:00:37,783 --> 00:00:40,455\nThe more confident they were in their own ability,\n\n11\n00:00:40,665 --> 00:00:42,877\nthe more critical thinking they reported.\n\n12\n00:00:43,047 --> 00:00:48,372\nIn most examples, workers felt that AI reduced the effort of critical thinking.\n\n13\n00:00:48,835 --> 00:00:51,357\nThat can free effort for higher level work.\n\n14\n00:00:51,684 --> 00:00:54,218\nOr it can mean the thinking simply stops.\n\n15\n00:00:54,388 --> 00:00:56,538\nCritical thinking did not vanish.\n\n16\n00:00:56,895 --> 00:01:00,643\nIt shifted: from gathering information to verifying it,\n\n17\n00:01:00,877 --> 00:01:04,611\nfrom solving problems to integrating AI responses,\n\n18\n00:01:04,848 --> 00:01:07,225\nand from doing tasks to stewarding them.\n\n19\n00:01:07,395 --> 00:01:09,385\nPeople also named the barriers.\n\n20\n00:01:09,691 --> 00:01:10,572\nLack of time.\n\n21\n00:01:11,097 --> 00:01:14,230\nA sense that thinking critically was not part of the job.\n\n22\n00:01:14,707 --> 00:01:19,524\nAnd difficulty judging AI output in areas where they lacked expertise.\n\n23\n00:01:19,859 --> 00:01:22,435\nSome even said AI added effort,\n\n24\n00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:24,789\nbecause its answers had to be verified.\n\n25\n00:01:24,959 --> 00:01:25,765\nA caution.\n\n26\n00:01:26,165 --> 00:01:28,366\nThis is a survey of self reports.\n\n27\n00:01:28,642 --> 00:01:31,245\nIt shows associations, not causes,\n\n28\n00:01:31,399 --> 00:01:34,588\nand people may not judge their own thinking accurately.\n\n29\n00:01:34,758 --> 00:01:35,520\nFor teaching.\n\n30\n00:01:35,894 --> 00:01:40,499\nMake verification visible and graded: ask students to show what they checked,\n\n31\n00:01:40,519 --> 00:01:41,269\nand how.\n\n32\n00:01:41,738 --> 00:01:44,249\nBuild their confidence in the domain itself,\n\n33\n00:01:44,343 --> 00:01:47,291\nsince self confidence went with more critical thinking.\n\n34\n00:01:47,753 --> 00:01:49,770\nAnd teach stewardship explicitly: deciding what the AI should do,\n\n35\n00:01:50,044 --> 00:01:53,914\nand judging whether it did it.\n\n36\n00:01:54,084 --> 00:01:57,459\nAI moves critical thinking from making to checking.\n\n37\n00:01:57,849 --> 00:02:00,152\nStudents still need to know enough to check.\n\n"
